#### 5.6.4 HIPAA and PHI Security

Micro-frontends handling Protected Health Information (PHI) must implement HIPAA Security Rule technical safeguards:

**PHI Encryption Requirements**:

```javascript
// Encrypt PHI before storing in browser local storage (AES-256-GCM)
import { encrypt, decrypt } from '@gainwell/encryption-utils';

class SecurePHIStorage {
  private encryptionKey: CryptoKey;

  async init() {
    // Retrieve encryption key from session (derived from authentication token)
    this.encryptionKey = await this.deriveEncryptionKey();
  }

  async storePHI(key: string, data: any): Promise<void> {
    const encrypted = await encrypt(JSON.stringify(data), this.encryptionKey);
    sessionStorage.setItem(key, encrypted);
  }

  async retrievePHI(key: string): Promise<any> {
    const encrypted = sessionStorage.getItem(key);
    if (!encrypted) return null;
    const decrypted = await decrypt(encrypted, this.encryptionKey);
    return JSON.parse(decrypted);
  }

  clearAll(): void {
    sessionStorage.clear();
  }
}
```

**Audit Logging for PHI Access**:

All PHI access must be logged with correlation IDs for HIPAA audit trails:

```javascript
// Audit logging service
import { v4 as uuidv4 } from 'uuid';

interface AuditEvent {
  eventId: string;
  eventType: 'PHI_ACCESS' | 'PHI_MODIFY' | 'PHI_DELETE';
  userId: string;
  patientId: string;
  resourceType: string;
  action: string;
  ipAddress: string;
  timestamp: string;
  correlationId: string;
}

class AuditLogger {
  async logPHIAccess(event: Omit<AuditEvent, 'eventId' | 'timestamp' | 'correlationId'>): Promise<void> {
    const auditEvent: AuditEvent = {
      ...event,
      eventId: uuidv4(),
      timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
      correlationId: this.getCorrelationId(),
    };

    // Send to centralized audit logging service
    await fetch('https://audit-api.gainwell.com/v1/audit-events', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: {
        'Content-Type': 'application/json',
        'Authorization': `Bearer ${this.getAuthToken()}`,
      },
      body: JSON.stringify(auditEvent),
    });
  }

  private getCorrelationId(): string {
    // Retrieve correlation ID from request context
    return sessionStorage.getItem('correlationId') || uuidv4();
  }
}

// Usage: Log PHI access when displaying patient claims
async function loadPatientClaims(patientId: string) {
  await auditLogger.logPHIAccess({
    eventType: 'PHI_ACCESS',
    userId: currentUser.id,
    patientId: patientId,
    resourceType: 'Claims',
    action: 'VIEW',
    ipAddress: await getUserIPAddress(),
  });

  const claims = await claimsApi.getPatientClaims(patientId);
  return claims;
}
```

**Session Timeout and Inactivity Detection**:

HIPAA compliance requires automatic session termination after 15 minutes of inactivity:

```javascript
// Session timeout manager
class SessionTimeoutManager {
  private inactivityTimeout: number = 15 * 60 * 1000; // 15 minutes
  private warningTimeout: number = 13 * 60 * 1000; // 13 minutes (2-minute warning)
  private inactivityTimer: NodeJS.Timeout | null = null;
  private warningTimer: NodeJS.Timeout | null = null;

  constructor() {
    this.initEventListeners();
  }

  private initEventListeners(): void {
    // Reset timers on user activity
    const events = ['mousedown', 'mousemove', 'keypress', 'scroll', 'touchstart'];
    events.forEach(event => {
      document.addEventListener(event, () => this.resetTimers(), true);
    });
  }

  private resetTimers(): void {
    this.clearTimers();

    // Show warning after 13 minutes
    this.warningTimer = setTimeout(() => {
      this.showInactivityWarning();
    }, this.warningTimeout);

    // Terminate session after 15 minutes
    this.inactivityTimer = setTimeout(() => {
      this.terminateSession();
    }, this.inactivityTimeout);
  }

  private showInactivityWarning(): void {
    // Display modal: "You will be logged out in 2 minutes due to inactivity"
    Modal.show({
      title: 'Session Expiring',
      message: 'You will be logged out in 2 minutes due to inactivity.',
      actions: [
        { label: 'Stay Logged In', onClick: () => this.resetTimers() },
        { label: 'Log Out Now', onClick: () => this.terminateSession() },
      ],
    });
  }

  private terminateSession(): void {
    // Clear PHI from memory
    securePHIStorage.clearAll();

    // Log session termination
    auditLogger.logPHIAccess({
      eventType: 'SESSION_TIMEOUT',
      userId: currentUser.id,
      action: 'LOGOUT',
    });

    // Redirect to login page
    window.location.href = '/login?reason=timeout';
  }

  private clearTimers(): void {
    if (this.inactivityTimer) clearTimeout(this.inactivityTimer);
    if (this.warningTimer) clearTimeout(this.warningTimer);
  }
}
```

**PHI Masking in UI**:

```javascript
// Mask sensitive PHI fields by default
function MemberDetailsCard({ member }) {
  const [showSSN, setShowSSN] = useState(false);

  const handleShowSSN = async () => {
    // Log PHI access
    await auditLogger.logPHIAccess({
      eventType: 'PHI_ACCESS',
      userId: currentUser.id,
      patientId: member.id,
      resourceType: 'Member',
      action: 'VIEW_SSN',
      ipAddress: await getUserIPAddress(),
    });
    setShowSSN(true);
  };

  return (
    <Card>
      <Field label="Name">{member.fullName}</Field>
      <Field label="Date of Birth">{member.dob}</Field>
      <Field label="SSN">
        {showSSN ? member.ssn : '***-**-' + member.ssn.slice(-4)}
        {!showSSN && (
          <Button onClick={handleShowSSN} size="small">Show Full SSN</Button>
        )}
      </Field>
    </Card>
  );
}
```

**Key HIPAA Security Requirements**:

- **Encryption at Rest**: Encrypt PHI in browser storage (sessionStorage, IndexedDB) using AES-256-GCM
- **Audit Logging**: Log all PHI access with user ID, patient ID, timestamp, action, correlation ID
- **Session Timeout**: Automatic logout after 15 minutes of inactivity
- **PHI Masking**: Mask sensitive fields (SSN, medical record numbers) by default
- **No PHI in URLs**: Never include PHI in query parameters or URL paths
- **Secure Transmission**: All API calls transmitting PHI must use HTTPS with TLS 1.2+

